\]

Work programme:

1) determine a fundamental system of relations between the \(1620\) arrows of the diagram, splitting \deleted{into} \(14\) \inserted{orbits} \deleted{\illegible{1}} under \(\unsure{\mathfrak S}_K\) (\unsure{with|with} \(542\) vertices, splitting into \(9\) orbits)

\margin{in particular, write all the arrows as composites of arrows ``coming from \unsure{relative|modular} dimension \(\leq1\)''}

\deleted{\unsure{2) Reduce}}

2) Take up the question again, eliminating the vertices of level \(0\) (except perhaps those of type \(\mathrm I_{10}\) ?),
\deleted{and \(\mathrm{II}_1\) (\unsure{which is deduced by} \(\mathrm{II}_1\) (which reduces \unsure{to those} of type \(\mathrm{III}_1\).) --- but Beware of the twist \inserted{\(\mathrm{tw}_{1/6}\)} \unsure{relatively|relational} : \(\mathrm{II}_1\) (\unsure{which gives an automorphism of the same type}))}

3) Eliminate in addition the \deleted{\unsure{skew}} ``tetrahedral'' pieces \(\mathrm{II}_1\) --- and all the pieces which do not seem to simplify the presentation of the relations.

